# Keep the Kiro agent out of the workshop materials, so it behaves like a fresh project
# grounded only by .kiro/steering. Attendees read these files on GitHub; the agent must
# not — reading them would let it skip ahead through the exercises.
#
# What stays visible to the agent (NOT ignored): .kiro/steering/, scripts/, corpus/*.pdf,
# pyproject.toml, and work/. That's the whole world it should see.
#
# ⚠️ .kiroignore is documented for the Kiro IDE; whether Kiro Web honors a repo-committed
# one is unverified (see ORGANIZER.md red tests), and there is an open bug where it can be
# read past. The "Stay out of the workshop materials" rule in .kiro/steering/workshop.md
# enforces the same boundary as a fallback — do not rely on this file alone.

modules/
setup/
provisioning/
images/
ORGANIZER.md
README.md
corpus/README.md
.agents/
